WEBVTT

00:02.547 --> 00:06.555
<i>As the quest judgment occurs right before Fuko and Andy,</i>

00:06.555 --> 00:10.062
<i>the failure to capture the Unseen Negator is told.</i>

00:10.479 --> 00:15.615
<i>Andy is confident that Unseen
was taken by Unrepair based on the clues.</i>

00:16.032 --> 00:21.251
<i>Signifying the existence of a Negator who may be an enemy,
the Roundtable goes silent.</i>

00:21.251 --> 00:28.808
<i>And then, as a penalty for not being able to complete all quests,
UMA Galaxy is unleashed into the world.</i>

00:29.267 --> 00:34.987
<i>Juiz mentions that penalties from Apocalypse all harbor
the possibility to drive humanity to extinction.</i>

00:35.112 --> 00:41.332
<i>Those words prove true as Acks, an alien race planning
on conquering Earth, brings a giant army.</i>

00:41.750 --> 00:45.633
<i>Juiz fends off the invaders using
her Negator ability Unjustice,</i>

00:45.675 --> 00:50.017
<i>and then orders contact with Negators
to fill the 11th seat of the Roundtable.</i>

00:50.434 --> 00:54.526
<i>Sensing an upcoming battle,
Andy volunteers to approach Unrepair.</i>

00:54.860 --> 00:58.659
<i>A new sunrise shines light down upon
the reddish soils of the land.</i>

01:01.999 --> 01:07.426
I'll go. If their ability is true to their name,
one attack'll prove to be fatal.

01:07.719 --> 01:08.637
I appreciate that.

01:09.013 --> 01:11.100
Fuko, you go along as well.

01:12.729 --> 01:17.237
Roger that. I gotta repay
the favor for helping me out!

01:21.705 --> 01:22.707
SEPTEMBER 8TH

01:23.709 --> 01:25.546
RIO DE JANEIRO,
BRAZIL

01:27.926 --> 01:29.554
LEBLON BEACH

01:33.646 --> 01:35.190
SHOPPING BLON

01:38.196 --> 01:39.533
MENSWEAR SECTION

01:48.258 --> 01:50.513
So many... celebrities.

01:52.099 --> 01:53.351
Sorry to keep ya waitin'.

01:53.561 --> 01:55.021
What took you so long, Andy?

01:55.021 --> 01:57.234
You know I don't fit in here.
I nearly died of embarrass-

01:58.988 --> 02:02.954
Y'know, it's been a while...
since I've gotten decked out in a suit like this.

02:02.954 --> 02:05.292
Well? Am I lookin' good, or what?

02:05.835 --> 02:07.881
Whoa. Such long legs.

02:07.881 --> 02:09.885
You're so chiseled, Andy.

02:10.343 --> 02:13.433
Y-Yeah! You look like some kind of ritzy celebrity.

02:13.433 --> 02:15.187
I'm not askin' ya what I look like.

02:15.605 --> 02:17.692
I'm askin' if you like what you see.

02:17.692 --> 02:19.403
Huh? Does that matter?

02:19.988 --> 02:20.865
It does.

02:21.157 --> 02:23.203
C'mon, how are the threads?

02:23.203 --> 02:26.417
- Good? Bad? Huh? Come on!
- Too close! Too close!

04:01.025 --> 04:02.696
A FEW HOURS AGO

04:05.660 --> 04:07.204
A black market auction?

04:07.956 --> 04:08.791
Yep.

04:09.125 --> 04:12.131
It's an auction that deals with Negators,
UMAs, and Artifacts...

04:12.131 --> 04:14.468
...that the organization hasn't been able to manage.

04:17.182 --> 04:22.902
Their operation's been busted up before...
but it looks like they're back in business.

04:26.075 --> 04:29.666
<i>The guys behind it are mafia
from all over the world.</i>

04:29.666 --> 04:33.465
<i>They always hold it in random locations,
so trackin' them down ain't no easy task.</i>

04:33.465 --> 04:35.177
<i>But Juiz managed to locate 'em.</i>

04:37.181 --> 04:40.563
The next auction will be held tomorrow at midnight...

04:41.022 --> 04:44.863
...on a luxury liner docked at the port of Rio de Janeiro.

04:45.489 --> 04:47.786
In Rio de Janeiro?
Could that mean-

04:47.911 --> 04:52.419
Location of Unrepair.
Right here.

04:53.421 --> 04:54.089
Yeah.

04:54.298 --> 04:59.643
We'll likely find Unrepair there.
Though, we don't know if he's buyin' or sellin'.

05:01.187 --> 05:06.322
We're gonna infiltrate the ship as guests using
these passes that Nico made.

05:08.201 --> 05:10.832
Infiltrate?
Are we gonna be okay?

05:11.165 --> 05:13.378
We can't show up dressed like this, of course.

05:13.378 --> 05:17.595
Only a select few celebs
are allowed aboard, which means...

05:18.096 --> 05:19.516
....it's disguise time!

05:24.651 --> 05:25.318
Oh?

05:25.485 --> 05:27.197
Whoa!

05:27.489 --> 05:29.034
S-So short!

05:33.586 --> 05:37.009
So, is covering yourself up some kind
of habit of yours?

05:37.217 --> 05:40.641
S-Shut up! It's your fault
for picking out all these skimpy outfits!

05:41.058 --> 05:44.023
Says the girl who was wearin'
a low-cut top when we first met.

05:48.574 --> 05:51.329
I planned on dying that day!
I just threw something on!

05:53.208 --> 05:56.213
That doesn't explain why you picked
nothing but skimpy outfits!

05:58.051 --> 06:01.349
We need the surface area
to make sure big strokes of unluck occur-

06:01.432 --> 06:03.353
Yeah, sure, a likely story!

06:03.687 --> 06:06.025
That might work for you,
but not for me!

06:06.025 --> 06:07.904
It might put other people in danger, too!

06:08.822 --> 06:09.908
What're you talkin' about?

06:10.116 --> 06:12.204
You're going to this shindig as my gal.

06:12.204 --> 06:14.876
I'm not letting anyone else lay their hands on ya.

06:17.047 --> 06:20.846
If you're too embarrassed about showin'
some skin to enjoy yourself, then fine...

06:20.846 --> 06:23.560
...but at least wear whatever you like when you're with me.

06:25.690 --> 06:29.071
Besides, you do know these guys
buy people with money, right?

06:29.071 --> 06:32.160
Hittin' them with a stroke of unluck
would probably do the world some good.

06:32.327 --> 06:33.037
Wha...?

06:33.329 --> 06:34.415
I can't do that!

06:34.415 --> 06:36.503
If I'm not careful,
they could end up dead.

06:43.224 --> 06:45.437
You slipped in another scanty dress?

06:45.730 --> 06:46.397
Tch.

06:49.904 --> 06:51.115
<i>Miss Juiz...</i>

06:51.533 --> 06:55.457
May I ask why you chose
to assign me to this mission?

06:56.417 --> 07:00.509
Our highest priority right now
is securing an 11th member.

07:00.718 --> 07:01.511
The one we want is-

07:01.636 --> 07:03.222
Unrepair, right?

07:03.306 --> 07:04.433
I'll go.

07:04.768 --> 07:07.815
I appreciate that.
I'll assign you backup for insurance.

07:07.815 --> 07:09.193
Take Tatiana along with you.

07:09.276 --> 07:10.780
Wait a-me?

07:11.280 --> 07:13.242
Fuko, you go along as well.

07:18.294 --> 07:19.756
Do you take issue with my decision?

07:22.010 --> 07:26.477
I can see the point of sending Andy...
and Tatiana, since she looks solid and tough.

07:26.477 --> 07:30.401
But why me?
I'd just drag them both down.

07:30.986 --> 07:34.451
I am simply acting in accordance
with my own vision of justice.

07:35.830 --> 07:40.881
<i>And my justice is to protect this planet
and the innocent people who inhabit it.</i>

07:42.008 --> 07:46.225
That is why I ordered Shen
and Void to kill you.

07:48.354 --> 07:52.530
I felt leaving you unattended
would endanger this planet.

07:53.322 --> 07:54.241
However...

07:54.617 --> 07:59.502
...seeing our recent fight with Victor-
no, Victhor-made me think.

08:02.717 --> 08:09.313
If we can manage to control that Unluck of yours,
it might just be powerful enough to kill God.

08:13.070 --> 08:16.578
But your power is far from sufficient
in its current state.

08:16.912 --> 08:19.208
Ragnarøk is drawing near, as well.

08:19.208 --> 08:25.512
For that reason, might I request you work with him,
connect with him, and do what it takes...

08:26.347 --> 08:28.267
...to fall in love with him?

08:30.063 --> 08:30.731
Huh?

08:33.654 --> 08:36.158
Okay, that's it!
I've had it!

08:36.910 --> 08:39.999
If this doesn't work,
then get Miss Juiz to take my place!

08:40.584 --> 08:42.838
Lookin' good!
I give it an eight out of ten!

08:44.676 --> 08:46.972
Be confident.
Hold yer head up.

08:48.850 --> 08:50.646
Arms to the side,
not in front.

08:50.646 --> 08:52.148
Wha...? Oh...

08:56.115 --> 08:59.079
All right, now that's a perfect ten.
Let's go with this one.

09:02.294 --> 09:03.922
Not too tight 'round the chest, is it?

09:03.922 --> 09:04.924
Maybe a little.

09:04.924 --> 09:07.220
We'll have 'em do a li'l tailorin', then.

09:12.065 --> 09:15.155
We send the luggage to the hotel, and...

09:20.916 --> 09:23.881
We've got time to kill,
so how 'bout a walk?

09:28.306 --> 09:29.391
Yeah!

09:36.238 --> 09:37.575
Aah...

09:37.575 --> 09:38.786
Hey, by the way...

09:40.330 --> 09:42.209
About that stroke of unluck the other day...

09:45.256 --> 09:46.968
Y-Yes, what is it?

09:47.637 --> 09:49.431
When am I gonna get some?

09:50.100 --> 09:50.851
Huh?

09:57.322 --> 09:59.577
Why're you runnin' away?
Stop right there!

09:59.619 --> 10:01.080
Got the hint!
I decline!

10:01.288 --> 10:03.585
Lemme get a meteor shower of my own!

10:03.585 --> 10:05.046
I knew it!

10:05.463 --> 10:08.929
Victor was the one who ate that, not me!

10:08.929 --> 10:12.185
I was the one who smooched ya,
so I deserved to take that one!

10:12.185 --> 10:14.983
Not my problem!
That was out of necessity!

10:16.235 --> 10:18.615
If it's not necessary...
then count me out!

10:18.866 --> 10:19.826
You dope.

10:20.034 --> 10:22.414
Think you can buy time
with some random stroke of unluck?

10:23.124 --> 10:27.424
Well, too bad.
Right now, I'm in Full Armor Mode!

10:27.508 --> 10:28.342
FULL ARMOR MODE =

10:28.426 --> 10:29.971
FULL ARMOR MODE =
WEARING CLOTHES

10:30.180 --> 10:30.973
Clothy!

10:31.182 --> 10:32.225
Sure thing!

10:32.392 --> 10:33.436
Serves you right!

10:39.406 --> 10:41.995
Hm? Wait,
is this gonna hurt me, too?

10:48.466 --> 10:52.098
Sorry about that, Clothy.
I'll give you a nice ball of yarn later.

10:52.892 --> 10:56.733
<i>A ball of yarn:
UMA Clothes' favorite food.</i>

10:57.359 --> 10:58.069
Oh.

10:58.277 --> 11:00.574
<i>This was a combo-type stroke of unluck.</i>

11:01.660 --> 11:07.797
<i>Combo-type: low potency strokes of singular unluck
occurring in a chain reaction-like style.</i>

11:12.138 --> 11:15.436
Sorry about that. It ended up being
a lot bigger than I thought it'd be.

11:17.399 --> 11:18.401
That guy...

11:18.861 --> 11:19.737
Hm?

11:20.446 --> 11:24.747
You know, Victor.
I don't know who he is.

11:24.747 --> 11:29.006
Hell, I don't even know who I am.

11:29.591 --> 11:32.470
Heard he said somethin' about him bein' the original.

11:33.932 --> 11:39.401
For all I know, it's true.
I've barely got any childhood memories.

11:41.573 --> 11:44.954
Without this card,
I can't keep myself together.

11:45.956 --> 11:48.377
He might show up again someday...

11:48.377 --> 11:51.091
...and try to attack you and anyone else near you.

11:52.093 --> 11:53.179
If that happens, then...

11:53.387 --> 11:54.682
Don't worry.

11:55.183 --> 11:58.982
If that happens, then I'll use my unluck
to save you as many times as you need.

12:00.193 --> 12:04.076
So long as you're in there, Andy...
However many times.

12:11.215 --> 12:14.346
Now, let's go!
We need to get ready for tonight!

12:15.139 --> 12:17.435
Yeah... you're right.

12:22.655 --> 12:24.993
My gloves are still off! I'm sorry!

12:26.161 --> 12:27.163
Wait, Tatiana?

12:27.707 --> 12:29.585
Oh, it's you, Fuko.

12:29.585 --> 12:33.969
Strange. According to my calculations,
I was set to drop near the port.

12:34.428 --> 12:37.142
Guess my unluck caused a detour, then.

12:37.977 --> 12:40.691
Well, whatever. I assume
the boss has filled you in, correct?

12:41.066 --> 12:47.913
In seven hours, you two will be going undercover
to board that ship while I infiltrate from elsewhere.

12:48.456 --> 12:51.796
The auction is scheduled
to commence after a cocktail party.

12:51.796 --> 12:56.013
You two will search for Unrepair from the inside,
and I'll cover the outside.

12:56.430 --> 12:59.102
I'm sure the place will be filled
with revolting sights...

12:59.436 --> 13:02.693
...but don't blow your cover until Unrepair is located!

13:05.699 --> 13:07.118
Oh, Fuko, take this.

13:07.870 --> 13:12.922
I heard you were going to wear a dress,
so I had Mr. Nico remodel the necktie that members wear.

13:13.422 --> 13:15.009
I hope it suits you well.

13:16.846 --> 13:18.307
Thank you.

13:18.558 --> 13:19.267
Oh!

13:19.476 --> 13:23.025
One more thing! Those forged passes
have you two down as a married couple.

13:23.944 --> 13:24.612
What?

13:24.779 --> 13:26.783
Put on a good act, you two!

13:50.747 --> 13:53.127
Shall we, my honey?

13:53.127 --> 13:56.258
Y-Yes... my darling!

14:06.948 --> 14:08.409
SEPTEMBER 9TH

14:08.409 --> 14:09.913
12:30 A.M.

14:09.913 --> 14:12.208
DEPARTURE FROM PORT OF RIO DE JANEIRO

14:25.193 --> 14:26.529
All right, heads up.

14:28.867 --> 14:31.246
We're about to enter the underbelly of society.

14:31.246 --> 14:33.710
Don't think about righting the wrongs around you.

14:33.710 --> 14:37.718
Just don't lose sight of what you believe is right.

14:39.388 --> 14:40.390
Let's do this.

14:40.599 --> 14:41.601
Okay.

14:54.292 --> 14:58.467
I simply must know how that Cryptid
you won in the previous auction fared!

14:58.467 --> 15:01.015
Aah... I wasn't able to use it at all.

15:01.683 --> 15:04.062
Andy, what's a Cryptid?

15:04.479 --> 15:05.774
They're likely talkin' about UMAs.

15:06.400 --> 15:09.657
I was actually thinking of cooking
it up sometime soon. Care to partake?

15:09.991 --> 15:10.826
Oh, why, yes!

15:12.495 --> 15:14.416
Don't listen.
It'll rot your ears.

15:17.338 --> 15:20.679
Did you hear? They say that a Negator
is the main item for this auction.

15:20.971 --> 15:22.850
Oho! Quite a rarity indeed!

15:23.267 --> 15:27.317
It's impressive they found one considering
how they just kill themselves off.

15:27.484 --> 15:30.281
Apparently, they're easier
to find now than ever before.

15:30.991 --> 15:32.410
Easier to find?

15:32.953 --> 15:34.749
The language unification must be to blame for that.

15:34.999 --> 15:37.963
<i>Unification of all the world's languages.</i>

15:37.963 --> 15:41.846
<i>Altering the memories and cultures
of all non-Negators.</i>

15:41.930 --> 15:45.103
All languages have now been unified to English.

15:46.856 --> 15:49.319
Ooh! Spotted some open seats!

15:51.991 --> 15:55.498
The only reason you and Shen can chat now
is because of that necktie, remember?

15:55.791 --> 15:58.922
Oh, I get it...
So, with Negators that can't speak English...

15:59.172 --> 16:04.141
Yup. With everyone suddenly chatterin' away in English,
they stick out like sore thumbs.

16:04.432 --> 16:07.982
Does that mean it wasn't a good reward for us?

16:08.440 --> 16:09.944
Not necessarily.

16:10.486 --> 16:13.743
The Union has a hell of an information network
of their own, you know.

16:14.119 --> 16:16.958
All we gotta do is be one step ahead
and secure them before-

16:21.801 --> 16:23.137
You ain't eatin'?

16:28.899 --> 16:30.569
But which is better?

16:31.278 --> 16:32.030
Hm?

16:32.030 --> 16:35.537
Bringing them to the Union...
or letting them be sold off here?

16:40.171 --> 16:42.217
Both are 'bout the same, aren't they?

16:42.217 --> 16:45.473
Ya either die during a quest,
or become some rich fat cat's plaything.

16:48.395 --> 16:52.529
I wonder what kind of person
is being put up for auction tonight.

16:52.988 --> 16:54.491
You curious?

16:54.951 --> 17:02.465
If they're an inconvenience to those around them like me...
then they've probably led a hard life.

17:06.933 --> 17:09.104
<i>Not knowing the logic behind their abilities.</i>

17:09.479 --> 17:13.195
<i>Not knowing what they should or shouldn't do.</i>

17:13.195 --> 17:16.201
<i>So I was about to choose death...</i>

17:17.453 --> 17:18.414
I used to think...

17:18.915 --> 17:23.591
Folks who ended up as Negators only
had three courses their lives could take.

17:23.925 --> 17:26.305
Accept their ability and lead their life.

17:26.639 --> 17:28.893
Fall into despair and choose death.

17:29.352 --> 17:31.858
Or double down and embrace a life of crime.

17:32.651 --> 17:39.497
But there's actually a fourth course.
And that's killing the source-God.

17:40.959 --> 17:45.092
I met you and joined the Union on a whim...

17:45.092 --> 17:47.514
...but I've changed my mind since meeting them.

17:47.514 --> 17:52.315
You don't need to accept, give up,
or double down on anything... you can fight.

17:54.069 --> 17:56.991
So that's why the Union's got my vote.

17:58.327 --> 18:00.832
What about you, Fuko?

18:01.793 --> 18:03.045
I...

18:03.420 --> 18:08.180
I can't accept myself,
and was even on the verge of giving up...

18:09.767 --> 18:11.938
But I would say that...

18:16.698 --> 18:18.325
Please stop troubling us, sir!

18:18.325 --> 18:21.331
This area is off-limits to non-personnel!

18:21.541 --> 18:25.966
Come on, do me a solid here, boys.
I want to show my girlfriend here the stars.

18:27.468 --> 18:31.644
You've been warned.
Guest or not, this is the last time.

18:31.644 --> 18:34.399
You think your pretty-boy looks
are gonna charm the mafia?

18:35.359 --> 18:36.529
Latla.

18:36.529 --> 18:37.363
What is it?

18:37.781 --> 18:39.033
Will I die?

18:39.325 --> 18:42.248
Yes, you take a fatal shot to the head.

18:42.875 --> 18:43.835
That so?

18:46.841 --> 18:48.887
In that case, I won't die.

18:50.599 --> 18:51.391
Oh, my.

18:51.391 --> 18:52.351
- Hm?
- Huh?

18:54.857 --> 18:56.861
<i>He cut our necks... in that instant?</i>

18:57.445 --> 19:00.660
<i>He even sliced the carotid artery?
Gotta stop the bleeding... stop the bleeding...</i>

19:01.871 --> 19:04.960
<i>Why can't I... move my hands...?</i>

19:06.046 --> 19:07.966
Th-Thanks.

19:09.219 --> 19:11.056
Kain! C'mere!

19:20.575 --> 19:24.374
See, Latla? If you weren't such a baby,
you could have snuck aboard like that, too.

19:24.834 --> 19:26.587
And get drenched in bile?
I think not!

19:30.135 --> 19:32.014
Rip, take this.

19:32.265 --> 19:33.100
Hm?

19:33.560 --> 19:35.187
Should I have brought a suit?

19:35.187 --> 19:39.572
No need. We'll be running amok anyway, right?
It won't matter

19:39.572 --> 19:43.120
Latla, you can toss that.
I don't need it.

19:44.999 --> 19:47.336
Well? Are there really any here?

19:47.336 --> 19:51.637
Yeah, just one, though.
We're going to take them now.

19:53.725 --> 19:56.146
And you thought we wouldn't find one, Latla!

19:56.146 --> 19:57.608
Your fortune-telling was way off!

19:57.608 --> 20:00.404
Shut your mouth.
That was sheer luck!

20:00.572 --> 20:03.118
Feng! Glad you could join us!

20:04.580 --> 20:08.462
He only speaks Chinese, Rip.

20:08.462 --> 20:11.552
Oh, yeah! Pardon me,
it slipped my mind!

20:12.261 --> 20:14.015
THANKS FOR COMING
Ganxiè ni de dàolái.

20:14.265 --> 20:15.560
NO NEED FOR THANKS
Bùyòngle.

20:29.212 --> 20:30.882
<i>We've got big trouble, Zombie!</i>

20:31.216 --> 20:32.719
- Not Zombie.
<i>- We have infiltrators on the deck of the ship!</i>

20:32.719 --> 20:35.850
- I told you, I'm Undead, ball brat.
<i>- They were speaking a language other than English!</i>

20:35.934 --> 20:36.602
- Huh?

20:36.978 --> 20:42.029
<i>A man with an eye patch slit a couple mafia necks,
and the victims were acting weird afterwards!</i>

20:44.117 --> 20:48.208
<i>There are four of them.
At least two are Negators!</i>

20:48.668 --> 20:51.507
They seem to be after
the Negator being put up for auction!

20:51.507 --> 20:52.884
What do we do, Boss?

20:53.553 --> 20:54.470
I see.

20:55.180 --> 20:56.767
Negator Hunters.

20:57.018 --> 21:01.401
This group has come up quite a bit as of late.
That is their unofficial moniker.

21:02.069 --> 21:04.282
Are these the same guys who took Unseen?

21:04.658 --> 21:05.618
<i>Most likely, yes.</i>

21:06.411 --> 21:11.463
<i>We share common ground in that they also specialize
in collecting Negators by force.</i>

21:11.922 --> 21:14.302
<i>But the difference lies in our objectives.</i>

21:15.137 --> 21:20.774
<i>We of the Union seek to kill God
in order to be freed of Rules.</i>

21:21.567 --> 21:22.861
<i>Them, on the other hand?</i>

21:23.738 --> 21:26.242
<i>They seek revenge against the world.</i>

21:27.537 --> 21:31.127
If the Negators they collect prove worthless,
they dispose of them.

21:31.127 --> 21:34.927
Well, I suppose we share
that aspect in common as well.

21:35.595 --> 21:36.931
We do not!

21:38.851 --> 21:44.111
The reason you tried to kill me
was to protect people, right?

21:45.865 --> 21:51.084
I know the powers of a Negator can be painful
and sad to deal with...

21:51.376 --> 21:52.169
But even if they are...

21:54.423 --> 21:57.096
That doesn't make it okay
to take it out on the world!

21:59.016 --> 22:00.102
Let's do this!

22:00.102 --> 22:01.271
Yeah!

22:01.271 --> 22:05.989
TO BE CONTINUED

23:36.002 --> 23:36.837
PREVIEW

23:36.837 --> 23:40.052
<i>There are those that resent the world because
of their ill-fated destinies.</i>

23:40.343 --> 23:44.978
<i>But the girl does not accept such resentment,
and harbors emotions that once saved her within her heart.</i>

23:45.187 --> 23:48.736
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 12-Activate.</i>

23:48.944 --> 23:50.948
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
